sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P0 as Administrator
    participant P1 as Web Application (System)
    participant P2 as Application Database
    participant P3 as Background Worker Meta Insights Sync
    participant P4 as Meta Graph API
    P0->>P1: openAnalytics(filters)
    P1->>P1: authorize administrator, validate date range and filters
    P1->>P2: read analytics settings, aggregate news, audience and engagement
    P2-->>P1: return summary, trends and post performance
    P1->>P2: read saved Meta snapshots and synchronization status
    P2-->>P1: return social metrics
    P1-->>P0: display dashboard, filters, charts and tables
    opt [inspect or change filters]
    P0->>P1: select post / date range / category / sort
    P1->>P2: query filtered data and optional post inspection
    P2-->>P1: return filtered results
    P1-->>P0: update analytics view
    end
    opt [export report]
    P0->>P1: export(scope, CSV or XLSX)
    P1->>P2: read report data for selected scope and filters
    P2-->>P1: return export rows
    P1->>P1: build CSV / XLSX
    P1-->>P0: download report
    end
    opt [synchronize social analytics]
    P0->>P1: requestMetaSync()
    P1->>P3: dispatch unique SyncMetaInsights job
    P1-->>P0: return to analytics
    P3->>P2: read selected connections and credentials
    P2-->>P3: return configured accounts
    loop [each connected account]
    P3->>P4: request daily metric series (last seven days)
    P4-->>P3: return points / provider error
    alt [valid data and unchanged account]
    P3->>P2: upsert snapshots, set ready and synced timestamp
    else [failure or no data]
    P3->>P2: set unavailable / no_data, preserve prior snapshots
    end
    end
    P0->>P1: refreshAnalytics()
    P1->>P2: read stored snapshots and status
    P2-->>P1: return updated saved metrics
    P1-->>P0: display refreshed social analytics
    end
    Note over P0,P4: Disconnected connections are skipped and marked disconnected. Queue execution depends on its configured driver. Reports read snapshots, not live Meta calls. PostPerformance supplies actual post statistics, the generic engagement widget remains a placeholder.
